User: {'Id': 37048, 'Reputation': 106, 'CreationDate': '2014-01-08 20:00:53.0', 'DisplayName': 'nigelc', 'LastAccessDate': '2014-09-13 05:34:37.0', 'WebsiteUrl': None, 'Location': 'New Zealand', 'AboutMe': "<p>One-man-shop landscape architect (BLA) based in New Zealand's far south specialising in landscape design and planning for rural clients (farms &amp; large lifestyle), especially planted and technical solutions for storm-water, farm runoff &amp; riparian, as well as urban design and townhouse work.</p>\n\n<p>I'm fluent in weed-science and ecology, urban trees, perennials/herbs, and NZ natives. With hard landscape I focus on geotextile applications and permeable surfaces such as gravel-grass, LIUD and open stormwater systems.</p>\n\n<p>I have a deeper background in materials and fabrication; mold-making, plastics, panelbeating, woodwork, concrete and construction, all of which helps with the hard side of landscape design, as well as providing an understanding of the culture that leads to pollution.</p>\n\n<p>I work from a tiny (pop. 22), remote place (nearest town 60km), and the net makes my life and business here possible.</p>\n", 'Views': 2, 'UpVotes': 0, 'DownVotes': 0, 'AccountId': 2507839, 'Age': None, 'ProfileImageUrl': 'http://i.stack.imgur.com/KobH3.jpg'}
