User: {'Id': 37220, 'Reputation': 101, 'CreationDate': '2014-01-12 16:50:14.0', 'DisplayName': 'Matthew Skelton', 'LastAccessDate': '2014-01-13 01:25:33.0', 'WebsiteUrl': 'http://matthewskelton.net/', 'Location': None, 'AboutMe': '<p>Matthew Skelton has been building, deploying and operating commercial software systems since 1998. He has engineered software systems for organisations such as London Stock Exchange, TUI Travel, Virgin Mobile and GlaxoSmithKline, as well as for MRI brain scanners and oil &amp; gas exploration.</p>\n\n<p>He is responsible for Build and Deployment at <a href="http://www.thetrainline.com/" rel="nofollow">thetrainline.com</a>, the UK\'s leading vendor of rail tickets, which operates one of the busiest web infrastructures in the UK. He is writing a book on <a href="http://softwareoperability.com/" rel="nofollow">software operability</a>.</p>\n\n<p>Recent speaking engagements include: <a href="http://devopssummit.com/" rel="nofollow">DevOpsSummit 2013 (London)</a>; DevOps Days 2010 (Hamburg); Internet World 2011 (London); and Sitecore DreamcoreEU 2011 (London).</p>\n\n<p>Matthew blogs at <a href="http://matthewskelton.net/" rel="nofollow">http://matthewskelton.net/</a> and is on Twitter at <a href="https://twitter.com/matthewpskelton" rel="nofollow">@matthewpskelton</a></p>\n', 'Views': 0, 'UpVotes': 0, 'DownVotes': 0, 'AccountId': 1303855, 'Age': None, 'ProfileImageUrl': 'https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2814cc20402299cffb1e46898424e84f?s=128&d=identicon&r=PG'}
