User: {'Id': 37783, 'Reputation': 101, 'CreationDate': '2014-01-24 08:35:11.0', 'DisplayName': 'Koushik', 'LastAccessDate': '2014-01-27 05:08:21.0', 'WebsiteUrl': 'http://stackoverflow.com/users/1825795/koushik', 'Location': 'Bangalore, India', 'AboutMe': '<p>curious and here to learn.</p>\n\n<p>"...But, you see, I was not trying to program in C++, I was trying to find the right way to deal with software..."\n--Alexander Stepanov</p>\n\n<p><a href="http://xkcd.com/1319/" rel="nofollow">nice1</a></p>\n\n<p>My interests are C, C++, lately Haskell and Python.\nAt work i use LabVIEW. I also know java but I feel bored with it :-)</p>\n\n<hr>\n\n<p>Useful links : </p>\n\n<p><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loop_optimization" rel="nofollow">Loop_optimization</a><br>\n<a href="http://www.ni.com/white-paper/3024/en/" rel="nofollow">State Machine Architecture(labview)</a> - a very good design pattern in labview(my favourite)<br>\n<a href="http://www10.informatik.uni-erlangen.de/~pflaum/pflaum/ProSeminar/meta-art.html" rel="nofollow">TMP(Todd Veldhuizen)</a><br>\n<a href="http://www.sgi.com/tech/stl/" rel="nofollow">STL(SGI)</a> - a must read doc. The best reference on how to design, organise and document your code in my opinion.<br>\n<a href="http://apps.nrbook.com/c/index.html" rel="nofollow">Numerical recepies in c</a> - An awesome book but requires significant amount of time to read.<br>\n<a href="http://www.youtube.com/user/BoostCon" rel="nofollow">BoostCon at youtube</a><br>\n<a href="http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/" rel="nofollow">Boost</a></p>\n', 'Views': 0, 'UpVotes': 1, 'DownVotes': 0, 'AccountId': 2045667, 'Age': 25, 'ProfileImageUrl': 'http://i.stack.imgur.com/mt5TX.png'}
